```cpp
static inline void process_blend (CFF2CSInterpEnv &env, PARAM& param)
{
    unsigned int n, k;

    env.process_blend ();
    k = env.get_region_count ();
    n = env.argStack.pop_uint ();
    /* copy the blend values into blend array of the default values */
    unsigned int start = env.argStack.get_count () - ((k+1) * n);
    for (unsigned int i = 0; i < n; i++)
      env.argStack[start + i].set_blends (n, i, k, &env.argStack[start + n + (i * k)]);

    /* pop off blend values leaving default values now adorned with blend values */
    env.argStack.pop (k * n);
}
```

The `region_count` comes from `varStore->varStore.get_region_index_count(get_ivs())`, which returns `regionIndices.len` of the VarData at index `ivs`.

The problem: if `k` (region_count) is large and the stack doesn't have enough items, then `start + n + (i * k)` can overflow or exceed the stack array bounds. The argStack has a fixed capacity (likely 48 or 513 elements based on CFF spec, let me check).

Actually, looking at the crash description again: "Global-buffer-overflow READ 8" - this is reading from a global buffer. The argStack is likely a fixed-size array. Let me check."}
